{
  "title": "BankLens REST Bridge",
  "uid": "banklens-bridge",
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": { "from": "now-15m", "to": "now" },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Request rate by route",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(banklens_bridge_requests_total[1m])) by (route)",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Error rate (non-200) by route",
      "description": "F18 — the `status` label's meaning: 400 is the CALLER's fault (a bad param, an unknown persona — bridge_server.py's _route_request maps ValueError/KeyError here) and is informational, not page-worthy on its own. 401/403 are auth. 429 is the bridge's own rate limiter. 500 is a genuine SERVER fault (everything else — a missing data file, an unhandled None in a transform, a real bug) and is what panel 6 below isolates and what the BridgeInternalServerError Prometheus alert (platform/observability/prometheus/rules/bridge-alerts.yml) fires on. Before F18, every non-2xx here — including real server faults — was reported as 400, so this panel could never distinguish 'a user typo'd a cert' from 'the service is broken.'",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(banklens_bridge_requests_total{status!=\"200\"}[1m])) by (route, status)",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}} ({{status}})",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "p50 / p95 / p99 latency by route",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(banklens_bridge_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, route))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{route}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(banklens_bridge_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, route))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{route}}",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(banklens_bridge_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, route))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{route}}",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s" }, "overrides": [] }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Total requests handled",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(banklens_bridge_requests_total)",
          "legendFormat": "total",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "none" }, "overrides": [] }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Bridge process up",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "up{job=\"banklens-bridge\"}",
          "legendFormat": "up",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "DOWN", "color": "red" }, "1": { "text": "UP", "color": "green" } } }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "5xx (server fault) rate",
      "description": "F18 — isolated from panel 2's full non-200 breakdown because a 5xx is never the caller's fault and should be visually impossible to miss: a real transform bug, a missing data file, an unhandled exception. Backed by the same BridgeInternalServerError Prometheus alert rule (platform/observability/prometheus/rules/bridge-alerts.yml) that pages on any 500 — this panel is what that alert is watching. Should read exactly 0 in a healthy system; correlate a nonzero value with the request_id in bridge_server.py's structured JSON log (F17) to find the exact failing request and its traceback.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "banklens-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(banklens_bridge_requests_total{status=\"500\"}[1m])) by (route)",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "color": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "red" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "red", "value": 0.001 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    }
  ]
}
